## 2. Proposed exact reduction of the flat magnetic ground energy

Label B occupancy pairs by X. At each X, the unique minus charge can occupy
any of |A|+2 occupied sites. Each allowed four-hop return path permutes these
color positions between X and Y; it is a permutation matrix with norm one.
Let Q_occ be the nonnegative spinless occupancy matrix obtained by counting
all such paths with coefficient two. The norm bound on each permutation gives

    <v,-M_full(0)v> <= <u,Q_occ u>, u_X=||v_X||.

The vector uniform over the minus position is preserved by every permutation,
so Q_occ is also an invariant subspace of the full color matrix. Therefore
the proposed equality is lambda_min(M_full(0))=-rho(Q_occ). This is a
kinematic reduction to prove from the supplied paths, not an added spin axiom.

For an A pair (a,c), let m(d) count outward assignments to the unordered
distinct B pair d. For input occupancy X, allowed d are disjoint from X.
The intermediate occupied B set is Y=X union d. Returning via any pair
d' subset Y with m(d')>0 gives X'=Y minus d' and contributes 2 m(d)m(d').
The vacuum contribution is 2 sum_d m(d)². If X is disjoint from the two
neighbor stars, the contribution is only that scalar on X. Thus Q_occ minus
the vacuum scalar is computable from finitely many pairs near X.

